.TH "CSSTRANSFORMCOMPONENT.IS2D" "3JS" "September 10, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
CSSTransformComponent.is2D \- CSSTransformComponent: is2D property
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]is2D\f[B]\f[R] property of the
\f[CR]CSSTransformComponent\f[R] interface represents whether the
transform is 2D or 3D.
.SH VALUE
A boolean.
\f[CR]true\f[R] if the transform is a 2D transform, \f[CR]false\f[R] if
it is a 3D transform.
.SH DESCRIPTION
The property can be both read and written, and is used in other methods
to determine the form of the output.
.PP
For example, if the component represents \f[CR]CSSRotate\f[R] and
\f[CR]is2D\f[R] is \f[CR]false\f[R], then the string returned by
\f[CR]CSSTransformComponent.toString()\f[R] will be in the form of the
CSS transformation \f[CR]rotate3d()\f[R] function.
If the value is \f[CR]true\f[R], the string returned will be in the form
of the 2\-dimensional \f[CR]rotate()\f[R] function.
.PP
More generally, when \f[CR]is2D\f[R] is \f[CR]true\f[R], any attributes
of the component that are only relevant to 3D transforms (such as
\f[CR]CSSTranslate.z\f[R]) are ignored, and have no effect on the
component\(cqs serialization
(\f[CR]CSSTransformComponent.toString()\f[R]) or its \f[CR]matrix\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Reading and setting is2D
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] translate = \f[B]new\f[R] CSSTranslate(CSS.px(10), CSS.px(20), CSS.px(30));

console.log(translate.is2D); \f[I]// false\f[R]
console.log(translate.toString()); \f[I]// \(dqtranslate3d(10px, 20px, 30px)\(dq\f[R]

translate.is2D = \f[B]true\f[R];

console.log(translate.toString()); \f[I]// \(dqtranslate(10px, 20px)\(dq\f[R]
console.log(translate.z.toString()); \f[I]// \(dq30px\(dq \(em z is still set, just ignored\f[R]
.EE
